Let me use Zepto — the 10-minute grocery delivery app. Millions of Indian users. Large engineering team. Handles exactly the kind of data DPDPA governs.

What Zepto collects from you

When you sign up and use Zepto, their systems collect and process:

Mobile number — for OTP login
Full name — for delivery
Delivery address — precise location
Payment details — UPI ID, saved cards
Order history — what you buy, when, how often
Device location — real-time while ordering
Browsing behaviour — what you searched, what you viewed
Age — sometimes inferred from purchase patterns
Health-adjacent data — if you buy medicines, baby products, diet food

That is a significant amount of personal data under DPDPA. Some of it is regular personal data. Some of it — health-adjacent, precise location, financial — borders on special category.

